+The myron no-monitor overlay also handles an exhausted constant prefix. After
+checking whole-page zero padding, it may place a single 8-byte initializer
+(`__LASTDATA_CONST,__mod_init_func`) in the final zero-filled bytes of the
+native `__DATA_CONST` page. The two segment extents remain disjoint and their
+combined end stays 4 KiB aligned. XNU maps that shared page through native
+`__DATA_CONST`; retained kext constants start on the next page. The fallback
+requires RO/NX Mach-O permissions, pointer-only relocations and preserved
+section alignment, and rejects live bytes, symbols or references in discarded
+padding. Existing fitting layouts remain unchanged. The emission report records
+`native_constant_marker_shared_page`; this is not a hardware qualification.
 
